  "description": "This proposal outlines plans to join the ground floors of two adjacent Grade II listed buildings, harmonizing their spaces for improved accessibility and functionality. The primary objective is to create an internal opening in the boundary wall between the buildings, facilitating easy movement from one structure to another at the ground floor level, while safeguarding the historical significance of both structures. A secondary objective is to strip out all internal non-structural partitions in 103 Worship Street. It is not proposed to make any changes to the external appearance of either property.",
